{
  "$comment": "PLACEHOLDER RECORDS — the form definitions. Stands in for GET /api/v1/admin/resources and GET /api/v1/admin/resources/{id}. A resource is a FORM plus the DEPARTMENT it is for. `departments[]` is the whole audience rule — a member in ANY of them is in the audience and it is evaluated at read time against the team roster, never materialised into a list of ids — the day somebody joins Sales they are inside the Sales onboarding audience without anybody re-sending anything. An EMPTY list is every active member, not none: the difference between a company-wide form and one that goes nowhere is an empty string, and `audienceOf` in views/Resources/store.ts is the one place that reading is enforced. `tags` is free text, not an enum — `vocabularies.json` seeds suggestions and never a closed list. `version` is what makes an answered form safe to edit: bump it and old responses keep pointing at the version they answered. `fields[].accept` is a `file` field's allowed types (empty = any) and `fields[].maxMb` its size cap in megabytes (null = uncapped); both are printed to the member before they open a file picker, and both must be enforced server-side.",
